# 0.1.18: off the boots' surface (a PCVR tester on 0.1.17: "magnetic surface controls break the walking directions even
# after you fall of the walk area"). magnetturn.sim's walk up Batalia's magnet wall, square on, the stick held on past
# where the strip leans off to -y near its top (about z 44), where he slips off and falls; then on the ground below the
# head turns left and back (3400 on), and at the end walks straight, the stick ahead. The view's up follows the
# surface by arcs a frame at a time, and coming off it can be left turned about up; from 0.1.18 the rig takes that turn
# ([vr-boots] off the surface: ... degrees), so the stick, throws and the room's steps go where the view looks again.
# QUEST_WALK_TRACE: his step along and across his facing each tick, "aim" where the stick's ahead goes and "view" where the
# drawn view looks: the same from the moment he is off. With QUEST_TEST_NO_BOOTS_FOLD=1 the turn is left as 0.1.17 left
# it: "view" stays off "aim" by what the fold line would have said. He walks straight for some 25 ticks, then meets a wall:
# the two walk shots are in those ticks. QUEST_STATE_TRACE: states and places.
